WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.806
Prime Minister Mark Carney holds six point eight million dollars in Brookfield Asset Management options.

00:00:05.806 --> 00:00:09.727
Brookfield manages over ten trillion dollars in assets globally.

00:00:09.727 --> 00:00:15.579
Carney pitched a fifty-billion-dollar fund to Brookfield — documented in lobbyist registry data.

00:00:15.579 --> 00:00:20.443
His Cabinet participation requires a one-hundred-and-three-entity corporate recusal screen.

00:00:20.443 --> 00:00:27.568
A former Blackrock executive serves as Deputy Minister — creating additional entanglement between public office and private capital.

00:00:27.568 --> 00:00:33.170
The Parliamentary Budget Officer calculated MAID saves one hundred and forty-nine million dollars per year.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.761
Brookfield owns seniors housing globally.

00:00:35.761 --> 00:00:41.977
MAID expansion reduces demand for long-term care — directly benefiting institutional owners of seniors housing.

00:00:41.977 --> 00:00:44.056
The financial incentives are aligned.

00:00:44.056 --> 00:00:45.999
The conflicts are documented.

00:00:45.999 --> 00:00:50.409
The question is whether they are coincidental — and the data suggests they are not.
